WEBVTT

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.900
We're going down
with this ship!

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.910
But we can't
let you kids die!

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.070
Not until you've
fulfilled your mission!

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.280
Not much time left...

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.380
All right, shake a leg!
We're ready to evac you now!

00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:35.060
Keep the Komusai from
being hit, no matter what!

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:38.560
Komusai ready to launch, sir!

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.300
They have the numerical
advantage for now...

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:45.140
...but we Zeon will definitely
beat the Federation in the end!

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:50.340
I'm sure you kids can see that.
Now get going!

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:29.150
Come on.
Careful you don't trip.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:30.220
'Kay!

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:34.080
Look, I said you could have two
for the price of one, right?

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:36.950
I was just hoping we
could make it three.

00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:50.510
<i>It was UC double-oh...</i>
<i>Double-oh whatever it was.</i>

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:53.070
<i>Anyway, the war was over.</i>

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:56.600
<i>Giant weapons had become</i>
<i>lifeless hunks of metal.</i>

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:05.680
<i>All that remained</i>
<i>on battlefields...</i>

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:08.150
<i>...abandoned by the soldiers</i>
<i>were feelings of emptiness.</i>

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:12.190
<i>Our team had disbanded.</i>

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:14.800
<i>Its members were all</i>
<i>sent to different places...</i>

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:17.390
<i>...as part of the post-war</i>
<i>reorganization.</i>

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.860
<i>As the only one</i>
<i>who was discharged...</i>

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:21.900
<i>...I carried on the</i>
<i>hope of the others.</i>

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:25.660
<i>That our team commander,</i>
<i>who had disappeared...</i>

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:27.710
<i>He still has to be alive.</i>

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:56.190
Christ... How long are
you gonna pine for her?

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:00.770
B.B.!

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:03.700
Quit crying
over her already.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:15.150
Beautiful things...
I hate them now.

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:23.890
What's that?

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:31.240
A hatch...

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:33.700
From a spaceship.

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:35.440
Spaceship?

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.980
A Zeon spaceship?

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:54.730
- Wait up!
- Quiet!

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:00.260
Is it safe?

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:04.900
Looks like someone's
been living in here.

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:08.680
Zeon soldiers?

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:16.610
"Doctor Flanagan"?

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:20.080
C'mon, I think we should
get out of here.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:23.850
This place is seriously
creeping me out!

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:32.530
S- Somebody's out there!

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:35.470
Yeah, I know. Check it out.

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:39.570
Footprints...

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:41.870
And besides that... Look.

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:43.640
Dog tags!

00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:45.980
That many?!

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:50.180
S- Somebody's definitely
living here!

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:52.050
Kiki, this isn't good.

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:56.260
A swan?
What's that doing here?

00:04:58.630 --> 00:05:00.650
We'll camp in here tonight.

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:03.220
What? No way...

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:34.790
Get up.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:37.400
Who are you?

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:40.630
Hey!

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:44.800
Forget it.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:47.770
Who are you guys?!

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:51.900
Zeon! And this one, too?

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:54.500
We're taking you
to the commander.

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:55.910
Commander?

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:57.710
Who's that?

00:06:03.390 --> 00:06:05.190
This village...

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:07.230
Was it destroyed in the war?

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:10.130
The river's course
must have been changed.

00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:26.350
Follow me.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.880
A mobile suit...

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:35.250
Where are we going?

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:41.060
Graves...

00:06:54.410 --> 00:06:56.400
Rank and unit!

00:06:57.550 --> 00:06:59.670
Tell me your ranks
and unit attachments!

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:02.050
I'm just a civilian.

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:04.090
But you're a soldier, right?!

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:08.520
My name's Kiki Rosita.
And he's...

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:12.120
Yeah. I'm, uh...

00:07:13.130 --> 00:07:16.760
Right... Earth Federal Forces,
Far East Division.

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:20.530
Combined Mechanized Battalion.
08th mobile suit team.

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:24.940
Petty Officer Michel Ninorich.
Um, retired.

00:07:26.410 --> 00:07:27.970
Kiki and Michel...

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:29.570
Don't lie to us!

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:32.670
We're not lying! If we were out
hunting for Zeon stragglers...

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:35.380
...there'd be more than just
two of us! Don't get us wrong!

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:43.920
How long have you
all been living here?

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:45.960
Are you waiting
to be rescued?

00:07:46.390 --> 00:07:47.660
If you are, forget it.

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:49.860
You must know that
the Zeon lost, right?

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:51.130
Shut up!

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:55.160
If you do know, then surrender
to the Federal Forces now!

00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:57.560
Yeah! That'd be the best thing...

00:07:57.670 --> 00:07:59.330
No! We can't do that!

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.740
The war will start again.

00:08:01.810 --> 00:08:03.570
And when it does,
they'll use us again!

00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:06.510
Living here will
be more peaceful.

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:11.480
You must have had some really
bad times after being drafted.

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:16.450
But you have to face the problems
you have now, in front of you!

00:08:17.090 --> 00:08:19.560
You have little kids
and wounded people here.

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:21.360
And I don't see much
food here, either...

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:28.670
Get up! I'll have you
stay in one of our sheds.

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:32.760
Kiki...
I think you went too far.

00:08:36.710 --> 00:08:39.270
C'mon, untie my hands!

00:08:41.850 --> 00:08:43.820
Then at least give
me my booze back!

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:45.890
It's not like you'll drink it!

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:48.180
Are you still going
on about that?

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:56.490
Stay here and be quiet.

00:08:57.270 --> 00:09:00.030
All right! He's gonna
go get it for me?

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:02.260
Unlike you, I can
reason with them, Kiki.

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:06.640
Maybe he's gonna poison it 'cuz
you're such a pain in the ass.

00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:09.510
That's it!
Maybe these guys did something!

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:11.410
Huh? Did what?

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:17.420
Like get shot intentionally
like Eledore to be hospitalized...

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:21.350
...or deserted in the face of
the enemy like the commander.

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:24.380
What are you talking about?

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:28.220
And then they couldn't go back to
either the Federation <i>or</i> the Zeon!

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:32.200
That's it! They must have
crashed that spaceship!

00:09:32.270 --> 00:09:33.930
Huh? For what reason?

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:37.540
Why else?
To run away from the war!

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:40.440
Maybe they killed the pilots.

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:43.810
And the commander, too,
if they caught him here.

00:09:43.880 --> 00:09:47.610
Don't be ridiculous!
Shiro's still alive, remember?

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:51.140
Yeah... Yeah, I guess.

00:09:56.960 --> 00:09:57.890
Kiki?

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:08.100
Okay, hold your hands out
to me and I'll cut you loose.

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:10.860
With THAT?!
You're kidding, right?!

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:15.630
Come on, hurry up!

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:30.020
Ow! I've got blisters now!

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:32.060
Shh! They're here!

00:10:32.630 --> 00:10:34.360
What are they doing?

00:10:43.710 --> 00:10:44.830
That girl...

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:46.340
Did she die?

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:56.980
They'll see you!

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:11.860
Kiki!

00:11:16.540 --> 00:11:17.830
Hold it!

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:22.370
Don't you have any
pity for that girl?!

00:11:31.850 --> 00:11:33.320
I said hold it!

00:11:54.080 --> 00:11:56.340
This is a..."funeral"?

00:11:56.810 --> 00:12:00.340
Yeah. You shouldn't just
shovel dirt over somebody.

00:12:02.650 --> 00:12:05.550
Tell me, what relation
was she to you all?

00:12:06.520 --> 00:12:07.680
She was...

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:09.150
A best friend.

00:12:09.220 --> 00:12:10.550
A sister.

00:12:10.630 --> 00:12:12.180
A comrade.

00:12:14.130 --> 00:12:17.260
Well, then!
Why not look sad, at least?!

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:20.100
I don't get it! She was
your friend, right?!

00:12:20.200 --> 00:12:22.170
How can you all look so calm?!

00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:25.670
We're sad, but...

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:27.710
Our hearts are one.

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:29.940
Our minds are one.

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:30.980
Forever...

00:12:31.050 --> 00:12:32.600
...and ever...

00:12:32.680 --> 00:12:36.840
...she shall live on
inside of us. Forever.

00:12:38.120 --> 00:12:40.280
Isn't that right... Aina?

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:45.020
- "Aina"?!
- Are you saying she's?!

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:51.700
Do any of you recognize
the man in this picture?

00:12:53.570 --> 00:12:55.730
His name's Shiro Amada.

00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:59.600
If you know anything, anything
at all, then tell me, please!

00:13:04.910 --> 00:13:07.780
Is that the name
of a comrade of yours?

00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:10.550
Yes. Someone very
important to us.

00:13:10.690 --> 00:13:13.920
You know, don't you?!
Where's the commander now?!

00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:17.050
He's dead.

00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:20.890
That man is dead.
His grave is here.

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:22.860
You're lying!

00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:24.690
Don't you dare joke about that!

00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:27.670
What have you done
with our commander?!

00:13:27.770 --> 00:13:30.260
I told you!
Your commander's dead!

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:32.340
- You little!
- Michel!

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:33.810
What?!

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:53.390
Wh- What's your problem?!
What do you wanna do to me?!

00:13:57.230 --> 00:13:58.990
Weird kid.

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:02.260
What?!

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:08.900
It's cold...

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:19.620
No, not like that. See?

00:14:19.690 --> 00:14:22.780
You put the food on the
leaf plate, like this.

00:14:22.860 --> 00:14:25.220
Then you say
"Please, help yourself."

00:14:25.990 --> 00:14:26.760
That's it.

00:14:26.860 --> 00:14:28.230
Please, help yourself.

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:29.320
Okay.

00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:32.920
Mmm, it's looks delicious.
Let's eat!

00:14:36.070 --> 00:14:38.230
Ah, that was good!

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:42.310
You want to try
playing house, too?

00:15:03.930 --> 00:15:06.130
That girl Aina who died...

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:11.000
Who was she, really?

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:12.860
What's that supposed to mean?

00:15:12.940 --> 00:15:16.770
Aina wasn't that young.
She wasn't Aina!

00:15:17.410 --> 00:15:19.400
Tell me what
her real name was.

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:23.010
She didn't have one!
She was Aina! Her name was Aina!

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:25.990
I want you to
tell me the truth.

00:15:26.050 --> 00:15:27.990
You're hiding something,
aren't you?

00:15:28.060 --> 00:15:31.790
Shut up! The man you're
looking for is in that grave!

00:15:32.060 --> 00:15:34.960
Then tell me!
How did Shiro die?!

00:15:35.800 --> 00:15:36.820
Well, he!

00:15:36.900 --> 00:15:38.490
Did you kill him?!

00:15:38.570 --> 00:15:39.400
No!

00:15:39.470 --> 00:15:40.330
Then what?!

00:15:40.400 --> 00:15:45.070
Shut up! The man you're looking
for really is dead!

00:15:45.140 --> 00:15:47.130
Now get out of here!

00:16:06.160 --> 00:16:09.130
What are you <i>doing?!</i>
We don't need that many!

00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:12.860
Well, this way they can't
clobber me with one again!

00:16:20.680 --> 00:16:22.300
I think we should stop.

00:16:22.380 --> 00:16:26.570
No way! We won't get anywhere
until we see who's in this grave!

00:16:26.950 --> 00:16:28.810
Well, yeah, but...

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:32.320
But what if the commander's
really in here?

00:16:39.030 --> 00:16:41.190
Nobody's in there.

00:16:41.700 --> 00:16:43.820
Nobody's in there?

00:17:34.550 --> 00:17:38.080
We were at
Dr. Flanagan's institute.

00:17:38.650 --> 00:17:40.620
We don't know
anything before that.

00:17:40.690 --> 00:17:42.620
Not our families or our names.

00:17:42.690 --> 00:17:43.990
Not even your names?

00:17:44.060 --> 00:17:46.390
All they ever called
us was "you kids."

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:50.190
When the adults died,
we didn't know what to do.

00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:53.600
That's when we
met Shiro and Aina.

00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:57.360
They taught us all
sorts of things.

00:17:57.470 --> 00:17:59.840
How to build a fire,
how to fish.

00:17:59.940 --> 00:18:03.500
How to make drinkable water,
how to bandage wounds...

00:18:05.450 --> 00:18:08.780
Then they dug that grave and
buried their clothes in it.

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:11.750
They said "Now we're reborn."

00:18:14.590 --> 00:18:16.820
Now we're reborn...

00:18:17.960 --> 00:18:19.260
I see.

00:18:19.330 --> 00:18:22.060
After that, they gave us names.

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:23.490
Names?

00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:25.190
I'm Sanders.

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:27.670
I'm Eledore.

00:18:27.770 --> 00:18:28.260
Karen.

00:18:28.340 --> 00:18:29.360
Michel.

00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:31.270
She's Kiki.

00:18:31.510 --> 00:18:34.870
And Aina even gave that girl
her name to encourage her.

00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:38.940
That's so like the commander...

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:41.380
Kiki, take your name back.

00:18:42.280 --> 00:18:44.250
"Kiki" is your name.

00:18:44.990 --> 00:18:46.650
- Take them back.
- Our names.

00:18:46.720 --> 00:18:48.350
I'll give you back
your name, Michel.

00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:49.390
And me!

00:18:49.460 --> 00:18:51.190
No, don't!

00:18:51.660 --> 00:18:54.720
No! No! No!
I won't allow it!

00:18:55.330 --> 00:18:57.700
They're our names now!
We won't give them back!

00:18:58.430 --> 00:19:02.700
Shiro Amada is MY name now!
I won't give it back!

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:04.540
No way!

00:19:04.610 --> 00:19:05.630
That kid!

00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:07.870
- Don't be mad at him!
- I know!

00:19:21.860 --> 00:19:25.620
Shiro's my name! MY name!

00:19:27.160 --> 00:19:28.890
He gave it to me!

00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:33.100
Kid...

00:19:33.170 --> 00:19:37.230
I'm Shiro! I have a name!
Call me that!

00:19:37.300 --> 00:19:39.000
Call me Shiro!

00:19:39.770 --> 00:19:45.140
He gave it to me!
So you can't have it back!

00:19:45.210 --> 00:19:47.680
I'm the only Shiro here!

00:19:48.680 --> 00:19:50.170
Take your name?

00:19:51.850 --> 00:19:56.220
I won't do that.
There's no way I could, right?

00:19:59.830 --> 00:20:02.520
Trying to protect their names...

00:20:02.600 --> 00:20:05.190
You've tried so hard
to lead them yourself.

00:20:05.400 --> 00:20:07.560
Names are precious
to everyone...

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:10.000
...and you should never give
them away to anyone, right?

00:20:10.070 --> 00:20:11.770
But it's all right now.

00:20:11.840 --> 00:20:14.030
No one's going to do
that to you ever again.

00:20:19.880 --> 00:20:24.110
You're a great commander.
You deserve to be Shiro Amada.

00:21:04.020 --> 00:21:07.390
Snow? This is snow?
Michel, look at it!

00:21:07.460 --> 00:21:11.330
No kidding! How can you be
so happy when it's this cold?!

00:21:31.790 --> 00:21:33.250
Hey!

00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:57.810
Did the commander
teach them this, too?

00:22:00.410 --> 00:22:02.610
Jeez, that's just like him.

00:22:08.460 --> 00:22:10.580
So, where did they go?

00:22:12.790 --> 00:22:13.990
North.

00:22:14.090 --> 00:22:15.220
North?

00:22:15.330 --> 00:22:17.300
Why'd they go north?

00:22:18.330 --> 00:22:22.060
He said there's a new
world there. A new life.

00:22:23.300 --> 00:22:27.600
Jeez... You even talk
just like the commander.

00:23:05.110 --> 00:23:07.270
They're all gone.

00:23:08.120 --> 00:23:11.680
They disappeared?
While we were asleep?

00:23:12.050 --> 00:23:13.380
But how?

00:23:17.830 --> 00:23:20.790
I've been thinking about that.

00:23:23.660 --> 00:23:27.460
About whether it
was all an illusion.

00:23:29.200 --> 00:23:30.360
An illusion?

00:23:30.470 --> 00:23:32.670
Yeah, an illusion.

00:23:32.940 --> 00:23:35.570
And if it wasn't,
then maybe they were all ghosts.

00:23:35.640 --> 00:23:38.270
I don't think they were either.

00:23:38.350 --> 00:23:41.140
They must have gone
out searching, too.

00:23:41.220 --> 00:23:43.240
Searching? For what?

00:23:43.320 --> 00:23:48.250
What else?
For a new world. A new life.

00:23:48.520 --> 00:23:51.010
Yeah. I guess you're right.

00:24:45.980 --> 00:24:47.950
COMMANDER!!!

00:25:23.770 --> 00:25:26.950
arashi no naka de kagayaite
You see the dream shining within the storm.

00:25:26.950 --> 00:25:31.240
sono yume o akiramenaide
Hang on to it now! Don't let it go.

00:25:31.310 --> 00:25:34.800
kizutsuita anata no senaka no
All I want is to take those wings on your back...

00:25:34.880 --> 00:25:39.050
tenshi no hane sotto daite
Those wounded angel wings, and gently...

00:25:39.120 --> 00:25:42.650
daite agetai
...pull them close to me.

00:25:48.730 --> 00:25:54.960
aoku hatenai sora no katasumi de
Newborn in a corner of the endless blue sky...

00:25:55.040 --> 00:25:58.240
umareta yume ga
The dream is there,

00:25:58.240 --> 00:26:01.370
ima chiisakutemo
and even though it may now be small...

00:26:02.510 --> 00:26:06.240
koori tsuku you na
No matter how strong they may blow...

00:26:06.310 --> 00:26:10.220
tsuyoi kaze de sae
...or how icy they may be...

00:26:10.280 --> 00:26:13.990
sono mune ni kagayaku
...those winds can never erase...

00:26:13.990 --> 00:26:18.420
yume o keshitari, sou yo
...the dream that shines. Oh, no!

00:26:18.490 --> 00:26:21.930
keshitari nante dekinai
The dream that shines inside your heart!

00:26:22.030 --> 00:26:25.160
arashi no naka de kagayaite
You see the dream shining within the storm.

00:26:25.230 --> 00:26:29.360
sono yume o akiramenaide
Hang on to it now! Don't let it go.

00:26:29.440 --> 00:26:32.960
kizutsuita anata no senaka no
All I want is to take those wings on your back...

00:26:33.040 --> 00:26:37.200
tenshi no hane sotto daite
Those wounded angel wings, and gently...

00:26:37.280 --> 00:26:41.580
daite agetai
...pull them close to me.
